      "definition": "A predicted identity REACHES THE GATE when either of two things is true of the track the tracker actually returned: its anchor was observed inside the closed band of half-width 20 px around the gate SEGMENT (the same band geometry trafficlens.bench.baselines uses, so the foot of perpendicular must lie between the gate's endpoints -- a vehicle on another carriageway crossing the gate's infinite line past its end does not count), or its swept path crossed the bounded gate segment and the gate rule emitted a crossing for it. The second clause is not decoration: under decimation a vehicle can move further than the band's whole width between samples, and a containment test alone would report that it never reached the gate, collapsing the ratio for reasons that have nothing to do with identity.",
